            <ArticleTitle>8,4'-Oxyneolignane glucosides from an aqueous extract of &quot;ban lan gen&quot; (Isatis indigotica root) and their absolute configurations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>638-646</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.apsb.2017.09.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three pairs of glycosidic 8,4'-oxyneolignane diastereoisomers, named isatioxyneolignosides A-F (1-6), were isolated from an aqueous extract of Isatis indigotica roots. Their structures and absolute configurations were elucidated by comprehensive spectroscopic data analysis and enzyme hydrolysis. The validity of ΔδC8-C7 values to distinguish threo and erythro aryl glycerol units and Cotton effects at 235±5 nm to determine absolute configurations at C-8 in 1-6 and their aglycones (1a-6a) are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
